+## 2026-09-23 — Let the changing image carry the explanation
+
+The current chapter already joins the bodily encounter to its computational conditions: one canvas receives two inputs and keeps changing after a ball is returned. Kept every existing paragraph, code excerpt, artifact anchor and the Albers comparison. Added a shared four-state illustration captured from the working museum. Intent, tutorial and critical companion remain unchanged.
+
+The focused run passes 30 assertions using an existing pigment without brush overrides. Actual pickup, ray hits, rectangular UV conversion and release work; automation continues after manual input ends. A separate, explicitly labelled quiet-input diagnostic confirms image feedback and fading toward white. Supplied keys drive the ordinary controller to the tray and back. This does not establish headset comfort, physical hand reach, colour calibration or learner experience.
+
+The Albers capture shows several studies through the existing opening, not an unobstructed survey of all 98. It remains supplementary evidence. No production repair, live restart, live bake/save replacement or full-book/audio regeneration was needed. Before sources, native images, report and manuscript diff are preserved in doc/book/iterations/2026-09-23-paint-shared-memory/. Next: Color_Walls, where colour helps organise the room.
